ption: Analyze images using AI vision. Provides a comprehensive description and answers a specific question about the image content.\n   Parameters schema: {\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"image_url\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"Image URL (http/https) or local file path to analyze.\"}, \"question\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"Your specific question or request about the image to resolve. The AI will automatically provide a complete image description AND answer your specific question.\"}}, \"required\": [\"image_url\", \"question\"]}\n\n28. **write_file**\n   Description: Write content to a file, completely replacing existing content. Use this instead of echo/cat heredoc in terminal. Creates parent directories automatically. OVERWRITES the entire file — use 'patch' for targeted edits.\n   Parameters schema: {\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"path\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"Path to the file to write (will be created if it doesn't exist, overwritten if it does)\"}, \"content\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"Complete content to write to the file\"}}, \"required\": [\"path\", \"content\"]}\n\n--- TOOL SELECTION RULES ---\n1. Analyze the user's request carefully and determine which tool(s) can help.\n2. If multiple tools are relevant, choose the most appropriate one(s). You may call multiple tools in a single response.\n3. Ensure all required parameters are provided. If a required parameter is missing, ask the user for it instead of guessing.\n4. Do NOT make up parameter values. Only use values explicitly provided by the user or derived from context.\n\n--- RESPONSE FORMAT ---\nWhen you decide to use a tool, respond ONLY with a valid JSON object containing a \"tool_calls\" array. Do NOT include any explanatory text outside the JSON.\n\nFormat:\n{\n  \"tool_calls\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"call_unique_id\",\n      \"type\": \"function\",\n      \"function\": {\n        \"name\": \"tool_name\",\n  